WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.660
A Software Bill of Materials, or SBOM,

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:08.510
is a structured inventory of the software components that make up an application or software product.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:12.899
It helps organizations understand the ingredients inside software they build, buy, deploy,

00:00:12.899 --> 00:00:13.630
and maintain.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:17.287
A common comparison is an ingredient list on packaged food.

00:00:17.287 --> 00:00:21.309
The list does not tell you everything about quality or safety,

00:00:21.309 --> 00:00:24.600
but it gives you visibility into what is present.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.622
An SBOM plays a similar role for software components, dependencies, libraries,

00:00:28.622 --> 00:00:29.719
and related information.

00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:32.279
Modern software is assembled from many parts.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:36.302
A single product may include open-source libraries, commercial packages, framework code,

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:40.690
container images, build tools, and transitive dependencies brought in by other dependencies.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.346
Without an inventory, teams may struggle to answer basic questions.

00:00:44.346 --> 00:00:45.809
Which components are used?

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:47.272
Which versions are present?

00:00:47.272 --> 00:00:49.466
Where did those components come from?

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:52.026
Which products rely on a particular library?

00:00:52.026 --> 00:00:53.123
SBOMs support transparency.

00:00:53.123 --> 00:00:56.779
They help developers, security teams, procurement teams, compliance teams, customers,

00:00:56.779 --> 00:01:01.533
and executives discuss software supply chain risk using a shared set of facts.

00:01:01.533 --> 00:01:06.287
An SBOM is not a vulnerability scanner and not a complete security assessment.

00:01:06.287 --> 00:01:11.041
It is a visibility artifact that becomes valuable when connected to vulnerability management,

00:01:11.041 --> 00:01:13.966
secure development, procurement, compliance, and risk management processes.

00:01:13.966 --> 00:01:17.257
This course provides an educational overview of SBOM concepts.

00:01:17.257 --> 00:01:20.182
It is not professional legal, regulatory, compliance, procurement,

00:01:20.182 --> 00:01:21.645
or software development guidance.

00:01:21.645 --> 00:01:27.130
The goal is to help you understand what SBOMs are and why organizations use them.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:31.518
The most important mindset is that an SBOM is useful only when

00:01:31.518 --> 00:01:33.347
people can act on it.

00:01:33.347 --> 00:01:37.735
A clear inventory helps teams ask better questions, assign ownership, understand exposure,

00:01:37.735 --> 00:01:40.660
and make faster decisions when software risk changes.
